      "title": "Split the treasure",
      "goal": "Split the 10 coins between your two hands. How many can you put in each? Try a different split!",
      "emoji": "🪙",
      "count": 10,
      "zones": [
        "Left hand",
        "Right hand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 3: Taking away"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "**Taking away** (subtracting) means some things go away. You had 8 sweets and ate 3. Count back 3 from 8: 7, 6, 5. You have 5 left."
    },
    {
      "type": "chart",
      "kind": "number_line",
      "title": "Taking away 3 from 8",
      "caption": "Start at 8 and hop back 3 steps. You land on 5.",
      "from": 0,
      "to": 10,
      "marks": [
        8,
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "number",
        "prompt": "What is 9 - 4?",
        "answer": {
          "value": 5,
          "tolerance": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "true_false",
        "prompt": "If you have 5 pencils and add 0 more, you still have 5.",
        "answer": [
          true
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 4: Shapes and measuring"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "A **triangle** has 3 sides. A **square** has 4 equal sides. A **circle** has no corners at all. We measure how long things are with a ruler, and tell the time with a clock."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "How many sides does a triangle have?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "2"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "3"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "4"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "b"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 5: Patterns"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "A pattern repeats. Red, blue, red, blue, red, ... the next one is blue!"
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "What comes next? 🔴 🔵 🔵 🔴 🔵 🔵 🔴 ...",
        "hint": "The pattern is red, blue, blue.",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "🔴"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "🔵"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "🟢"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "b"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "reveal",
      "prompt": "Can you make up your own pattern with 3 different colours or shapes?",
      "answer_markdown": "Any repeating group works. For example: star, heart, moon, star, heart, moon!"
    },
    {
      "type": "brain_game",
      "game": "memory_match",
      "title": "Find the matching pairs",
      "goal": "Turn over two cards. Can you find all the pairs?",
      "emojis": [
        "1️⃣",
        "2️⃣",
        "3️⃣",
        "🔺",
        "🟦",
        "⭕"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "summary",
      "points": [
        "Counting in 2s, 5s and 10s is quick.",
        "Adding puts groups together and taking away makes a group smaller.",
        "Shapes have a fixed number of sides.",
        "A pattern repeats, so you can guess what comes next."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "style": "tip",
      "markdown": "When you are ready, start the quiz. It has 12 questions and takes about 15 minutes. Do your best. Everything you show us helps plan your next lessons!"
    },
    {
      "type": "glossary",
      "terms": [
        {
          "term": "check-in",
          "meaning": "A friendly game that shows us what you know. It is not a test."
        },
        {
          "term": "adding",
          "meaning": "Putting groups together to find how many there are altogether."
        },
        {
          "term": "taking away",
          "meaning": "Some things go away, so you count what is left."
        },
        {
          "term": "triangle",
          "meaning": "A shape with 3 sides and 3 corners."
        },
        {
          "term": "square",
          "meaning": "A shape with 4 equal sides and 4 corners."
        },
        {
          "term": "circle",
          "meaning": "A round shape with no corners."
        },
        {
          "term": "pattern",
          "meaning": "Something that repeats again and again, like red, blue, red, blue."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
